    {
      "id": "claim_c6babbffa7d0467f8db38e7441a2e9da",
      "statement": "Bookmark is a dataclass with fields id (int, required), url (str, required), title (str, default \"\"), tags (List[str], default []), and created_at (str, default UTC ISO 8601 now). to_dict uses dataclasses.asdict; from_dict tolerates missing title, tags, and created_at keys. It also exposes matches_tag, matches_any_tag (OR), and matches_all_tags (AND).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/core/models.py#L1-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00ddc2e3fd1eae27e875caa9ba39b7c4569206974b25f8d8d0c8de68ff849f48:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b788a716bb424affaedbf69d2a2e63c3",
      "statement": "Store is the single persistence abstraction: every mutating operation (add, remove, clear) and every read (load, count) is a full load->modify->save cycle over bookmarks.json with no in-memory caching. add loads the list, appends, and saves; remove loads, filters, and saves; count loads and returns len. There is no locking, so concurrent writers can overwrite each other.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/core/store.py#L28-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0bb74e06f749fbdc5d7126aa64703d523c30689847b8057dbb65e93bed4961a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba457d155c004f688025f2ddc1562775",
      "statement": "Store resolves its data file from LINKKEEP_HOME env var (default ~/.linkkeep/) and always uses bookmarks.json under that root. _ensure lazily creates the parent directory and an empty [] file if missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/core/store.py#L8-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fd87e312035bb0ba5ee7210465e586679dadb5ea98a57df48c20afd54e135876:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0cdf20814367426abea08657fb16a26d",
      "statement": "Store.next_id(bookmarks) returns max(existing ids, default 0) + 1. Because it recomputes from the current set, removing the highest-ID bookmark causes that ID to be reused by the next add (IDs are not guaranteed unique forever). clear saves [].",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/core/store.py#L28-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00ddac7fb90035ccda04e7b9c97378e2974edbf4fb91e1974a1ffc08631362a2:"
