    {
      "id": "claim_0baa6919849b44898cec27c299285184",
      "statement": "The API layer exposes Store via deps.get_store() as a FastAPI dependency that lazily initializes a module-level _store_singleton on first request and reuses it thereafter. The singleton caches the Store object, not the data, so each operation still does a full file read/write. reset_store_singleton() clears it for test isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/api/deps.py#L1-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7c7c0cc363b17d8ec906202fe464a73fabf0d53a569803cfd44e82d59f4faf3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_597ac7b183ce473f9e58d49fa169cc0b",
      "statement": "The API router is mounted under /bookmarks and provides GET /bookmarks (optional ?tag= single-tag filter), POST /bookmarks (201, returns BookmarkOut), DELETE /bookmarks/{id} (204 or 404), and GET /bookmarks/tags (tag counts via core.tags.tag_counts). There is no update (PUT/PATCH) endpoint. app.py also exposes a standalone GET /health returning {\"status\": \"ok\"}.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://linkkeep/api/app.py#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:789b050cf7efcb299601dbe1e7024e9e350e4d76a4acd12edc5bde37c5178599:"
